  "og_image_alt": "When Leaders Inherit a Culture They Didn’t Build: Every generation receives paths it did not build, and must decide whether they are worth continuing to walk. TheWrkShop, Leadership & Culture.",
  "scriptures": [
    {
      "ref": "1 Kings 15:34",
      "text": "He did evil in the eyes of the LORD, following the ways of Jeroboam and committing the same sin Jeroboam had caused Israel to commit."
    },
    {
      "ref": "2 Kings 10:31",
      "text": "Yet Jehu was not careful to keep the law of the LORD….He did not turn away from the sins of Jeroboam, which he had caused Israel to commit."
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "the_revelation",
      "label": "The Revelation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "After Jeroboam, Scripture keeps saying essentially the same thing."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "King after king:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Walked in the way of Jeroboam.",
            "Continued the sins of Jeroboam.",
            "Did not turn away from the sins of Jeroboam."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Jeroboam becomes more than a person."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "HE BECOMES A PATH."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s profound."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The next generation doesn’t have to invent the compromise."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Infrastructure already exists."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Priests exist.",
            "Altars exist.",
            "Expectations exist.",
            "Habits exist.",
            "Social acceptance exists."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "All the next leader has to do is:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "KEEP WALKING."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_lie",
      "label": "The Lie",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“I DIDN’T CREATE IT, SO I’M NOT RESPONSIBLE FOR IT.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You may not be responsible for creating what you inherited."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But once you see it:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "YOU BECOME RESPONSIBLE FOR WHAT YOU DO WITH IT."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s true in:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "families.",
            "businesses.",
            "churches.",
            "organizations.",
            "leadership teams."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You may inherit:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "dysfunction.",
            "debt.",
            "mistrust.",
            "racism.",
            "favoritism.",
            "fear.",
            "silence.",
            "poor leadership.",
            "broken communication.",
            "unhealthy theology."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You didn’t start it."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WILL IT CONTINUE THROUGH YOU?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s the question."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "paths_create_ease",
      "label": "Paths Create Ease",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A path exists because something has been traveled repeatedly."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s what culture does."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "It makes certain behaviors easier."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The first person lies.",
            "Hard."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The hundredth person enters a culture where lying is normal.",
            "Easier."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The first leader hides bad news.",
            "The next generation inherits reporting structures already designed to hide it.",
            "Easier."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The first person mocks vulnerability.",
            "Years later nobody even considers vulnerability.",
            "The path is established."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "CULTURE REDUCES THE FRICTION OF REPEATED BEHAVIOR."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That can be beautiful when the path leads toward faithfulness."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And devastating when it doesn’t."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_truth",
      "label": "The Truth",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "EVERY GENERATION MUST RE-EXAMINE THE PATH."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Not arrogantly.",
            "Not assuming:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“Everybody before us was stupid.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "They weren’t."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "We inherited tremendous wisdom from people before us."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But faithfulness cannot merely ask:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“WHAT DID THEY DO?”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "It must also ask:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "“WHAT DOES GOD REQUIRE OF US NOW?”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because inherited practice remains subordinate to revealed truth."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_audit",
      "label": "The Audit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "WHAT PATH WAS ALREADY HERE WHEN I ARRIVED?",
            "WHAT BECAME EASY BECAUSE EVERYBODY ALREADY DID IT?",
            "WHAT HAVE I NEVER QUESTIONED?",
            "WHAT WOULD FEEL LIKE BETRAYAL TO CHANGE?",
            "WHAT ARE WE DEFENDING BECAUSE IT IS BIBLICAL, AND WHAT ARE WE DEFENDING BECAUSE IT IS FAMILIAR?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHAT WILL CONTINUE THROUGH ME IF I DO NOTHING?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_surrender",
      "label": "The Surrender",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Identify one inherited pattern."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Don’t immediately attack it."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Trace it."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Who started it?",
            "Why?",
            "What did it accomplish?",
            "What does it accomplish now?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then bring it underneath Scripture."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "“WE’VE ALWAYS DONE IT THIS WAY”",
            "is historical information.",
            "It is not biblical authority."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "take_it_with_you",
      "label": "Take It With You",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "You may not have created the path. But you are responsible for whether you keep walking it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_prayer",
      "label": "The Prayer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Father,"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Give me humility toward those who came before me.",
            "Give me gratitude for what they built faithfully.",
            "But give me courage to examine what we inherited."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Show me where familiarity has become authority."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Help me preserve wisdom.",
            "Repair what is broken.",
            "And refuse to pass forward what should end here."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "In Jesus name,",
            "Amen."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "hidden_gems",
      "label": "Hidden Gems 💎",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "Jeroboam became more than a person. He became a path."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Culture reduces the friction of repeated behavior."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "You may not be responsible for creating what you inherited. But once you see it, you become responsible for what you do with it."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "What will continue through me if I do nothing?"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "“We’ve always done it this way” is historical information, not biblical authority."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "-TheWrkShop"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
